.next/
# Regenerated by every `next dev` and `next build`, and the two disagree: dev writes
# `.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts`, build writes `.next/types/routes.d.ts`. Because build
# rewrites the file before typecheck runs, a wrong committed value is invisible to CI --
# it just dirties every contributor's tree and rots unnoticed. Nothing reads the tracked
# copy, so don't keep one.
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
dist/
.turbo/
*.log
agentroom_graph_*.html
*.tsbuildinfo
*.lnk
apps/web/.claude/
bridge/.tmp-test/

